    "title"             "Let there be Light!"
    "description"       "[h1]Let there be Light![/h1]\nA comprehensive lighting and illumination mod for [b]Necesse[/b] combining enhanced torches with decorative outdoor lighting fixtures, offering superior illumination, wire logic control, full multiplayer synchronization, and high-performance [b]AutoTorch[/b] mod integration.\n\n[h2]✨ Features[/h2]\n[list]\n[*] [b]Better Torch[/b]: Emits [b]2x vanilla light[/b] (300 light level). Mountable on ground and walls. Can be crafted anywhere in handcrafting (4 Torches -> 1 Better Torch) and uncrafted back to regular torches.\n[*] [b]Steel Lamp Post[/b]: Industrial metal street lamp (350 light level) featuring dynamic spark particles and full wire control.\n[*] [b]Wooden Hanging Lantern[/b]: Rustic hanging wooden lantern (350 light level) supporting 4-way wall and ceiling directional mounting.\n[*] [b]Phoenix Lamp Post[/b]: Ultra-bright ornate gold lamp post (550 light level) radiating a magnificent warm amber glow.\n[*] [b]Abyssal Crystal Lantern[/b]: Supercharged tier-2 water lantern (450 light level, [b]3x brighter than vanilla water lantern[/b]) with floating wave physics, bioluminescent aquatic particles, and land/water dual placement.\n[*] [b]Full Wire Support[/b]: All outdoor and aquatic lighting fixtures turn off when receiving an active wire circuit signal.\n[*] [b]Global Engine Optimizations[/b]: Non-destructive patches optimize all vanilla and colored torches with direct static light updates and bitmask wire checks.\n[*] [b]Multiplayer Synchronized[/b]: Server configuration automatically synchronizes to connecting clients seamlessly.\n[/list]\n\n[h2]🏃 Travel-Optimized AutoTorch Mod Integration[/h2]\n[list]\n[*] [b]Dynamic Travel Stride & Velocity Lookahead[/b]: Projects placement ahead based on player movement vector (including diagonal traversal) and scales placement stride proportional to torch brightness.\n[*] [b]Full-Radius Spatial Scanning[/b]: Scans up to 20 tiles away to detect existing high-intensity fixtures (Phoenix Lamps, Abyss Lanterns), eliminating redundant torch clustering.\n[*] [b]Recent Placement Hysteresis[/b]: Prevents duplicate placements during high-speed travel (sprinting/mounts) while the lighting engine computes.\n[*] [b]Terrain Awareness[/b]: Intelligently places floating Abyssal Crystal Lanterns when moving over liquid/water tiles and solid fixtures on land.\n[*] [b]Configurable Priorities[/b]: Choose between BETTER_THEN_VANILLA, VANILLA_THEN_BETTER, BETTER_ONLY, VANILLA_ONLY, or ANY_LIGHT mode with customizable sorting (SLOT_ORDER, BRIGHTEST_FIRST, CONSERVATIVE_FIRST).\n[/list]\n\n[h2]🔨 Crafting Recipes[/h2]\n[list]\n[*] [b]Better Torch[/b]: 4x Torch (Handcrafting / Workstation)\n[*] [b]Vanilla Torch (Uncraft)[/b]: 1x Better Torch -> 4x Torch (Handcrafting / Workstation)\n[*] [b]Steel Lamp Post[/b]: 1x Iron Bar + 1x Torch (Iron Anvil)\n[*] [b]Wooden Hanging Lantern[/b]: 1x Any Log + 1x Torch (Carpenter)\n[*] [b]Phoenix Lamp Post[/b]: 1x Iron Bar + 1x Gold Bar + 3x Torch (Iron Anvil)\n[*] [b]Abyssal Crystal Lantern (Upgrade)[/b]: 1x Water Lantern + 1x Quartz + 1x Any Gem (Workstation)\n[*] [b]Abyssal Crystal Lantern (Direct)[/b]: 1x Torch + 1x Any Log + 1x Quartz (Carpenter)\n[/list]\n\n[h2]⚙️ Configuration[/h2]\nCustomizable in [b]settings/lighting/settings.cfg[/b] (light levels up to 5000, hues, saturation, recipe difficulties, and AutoTorch travel parameters).\n\n[h2]🔗 Source Code[/h2]\nGitHub: [url=https://github.com/mahardikamaulana/necesse-better-torch]https://github.com/mahardikamaulana/necesse-better-torch[/url]"
    "changenote"        "v1.0.0: Initial release with Better Torch, Steel Lamp Post, Wooden Hanging Lantern, Phoenix Lamp, Abyssal Crystal Lantern, wiring support, full multiplayer sync, and travel-optimized AutoTorch integration."
}
